1
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:05,810
Kirito?

2
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:10,430
Kirito?

3
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:13,550
Kirito?

4
00:00:13,633 --> 00:00:16,000
Just five more minutes...

5
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:17,390
Come on.

6
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:19,677
I know it's our day of rest, but...

7
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:21,380
You sleep too much!

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,580
Good morning, Yujiro. Good morning.

9
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:34,437
Wanna go into town today?

10
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:36,840
The sun's out, and the sky's gorgeous.

11
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,471
To you, I'm with yourself

12
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:36,740
Shining Sun My Diamond

13
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:20,998
Damn, that's yummy.

14
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:23,700
Can't you wait till we get home? No.

15
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:27,117
They taste better when
they're fresh out of the oven.

16
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,057
Wanna have a bite?

17
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:29,717
No thanks, I'm good for now.

18
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:30,630
Maybe later.

19
00:02:30,713 --> 00:02:31,543
Suit yourself.

20
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:34,940
Man, I can't believe how time flies.

21
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:37,780
We left Rulid, what, two years ago now?

22
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:41,000
Yeah, so much has
happened to us since then.

23
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:42,950
Let's see.

24
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:45,640
First, we went to Zakaria.

25
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:51,757
We got to hone our swordsman skills quite

26
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:54,428
a bit while living and
working on that farm.

27
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:29,500
We won the swordfighting tournament
together and joined the Zakaria garrison.

28
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:33,397
It seems like yesterday
we came to the capital

29
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:35,833
and made it into the Swordcraft Academy.

30
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:39,740
I can't get over how amazing
it is that we're even here.

31
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:40,880
Oh, come on.

32
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:44,440
It's been like a whole year
since we moved to the dorms.

33
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:47,267
You should be bored out
of your skull by now.

34
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:49,260
I guess so.

35
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:50,750
Kirito!

36
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:55,670
Lina!

37
00:03:55,753 --> 00:03:56,798
What a coincidence.

38
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:59,629
Hey, good morning, ma 'am.

39
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:00,550
Good morning.

40
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:01,920
We haven't met yet.

41
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:03,580
You were you, Gio.

42
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:04,901
Is that correct?

43
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:06,320
Um, yes, ma 'am.

44
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:09,317
There's no need to be nervous.

45
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:11,537
I thought you were going home for the day.

46
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:13,502
Yes, I was just there, actually.

47
00:04:13,660 --> 00:04:15,597
They sent me back to get some things.

48
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,357
Um, may I carry that for you?

49
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:18,660
That's very kind.

50
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:22,017
However, you're supposed to
be Golgaro Sobalto's page.

51
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:22,930
You're right.

52
00:04:23,013 --> 00:04:23,843
I'm sorry.

53
00:04:23,926 --> 00:04:24,756
I was out of line.

54
00:04:24,839 --> 00:04:27,840
As for you, you are my page, yes?

55
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:31,178
So tell me, why is it you
didn't offer to help first?

56
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:32,110
Busted.

57
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:35,277
Oh, honestly.

58
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:38,260
I appreciate your offer
to assist me. Really.

59
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:41,346
However, I'm almost
finished with my shopping.

60
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:43,357
Besides, this is your day of rest.

61
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:45,734
You shouldn't have to think about work.

62
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:48,840
Your duty as pages will
be over soon, anyway.

63
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:51,832
Once we graduate, it's onward and upward.

64
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:54,924
If anything, I wish I
could learn more from you.

65
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:56,712
Your words are too kind.

66
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:58,804
I am blessed to be your mentor.

67
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:04,031
Thank you for everything.

68
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:05,557
It was an honor knowing you.

69
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:07,120
And an honor for me, too.

70
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:09,570
Same.

71
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:18,037
What the heck are you
getting all flustered for?

72
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:20,944
I guess it's because Sword
Alina's so beautiful.

73
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:23,340
And she's kind of intimidating, too.

74
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,034
Yeah, you got a point.

75
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:28,711
I'm a nervous wreck when we
spar, because she's so intense.

76
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,838
Gogoroso can be pretty intense, too.

77
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,190
In fact,

78
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:37,557
even after all the training I've had with
him, I still can't score a single point.

79
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:38,470
Same here.

80
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:42,817
Alina's always two steps ahead of me,
and she's second seat in her class.

81
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:44,860
I wonder how strong Volo is.

82
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,437
He's in the first seat.

83
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:47,480
Pretty strong.

84
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:50,477
Can you even imagine
beating an upperclassman?

85
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:51,900
I certainly can't.

86
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:54,900
And that there's the problem, huh?

87
00:05:57,320 --> 00:06:00,700
Well, good night, Kirito. Huh? Oh, night.

88
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:10,526
After being stuck here
for the past two years,

89
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:15,287
I learned that in this world, your true
power wasn't just expressed in numbers.

90
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:19,220
Only three stats show up in your window.

91
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:24,320
Your life, your object control authority,
and your system control authority.

92
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:28,364
If your object control
authority's a low number,

93
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:31,680
you can barely even hold
a higher class weapon.

94
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:36,700
But if your stat's way bigger than
the weapons, it feels crazy light.

95
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:40,437
Your system control
authority stat That tells

96
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:42,917
you what kind of sacred arts you can use.

97
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,059
If you're low level, you
can only use simple spells.

98
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:50,600
But if you level up, you get
access to more sophisticated ones.

99
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:55,620
That's how it works in games too.

100
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:59,557
But there's an extra feature
here that affects your stats.

101
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:02,480
It's something SAO and AOLO didn't have.

102
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:07,769
Sometimes the strength of a mental image
you create can influence your stats.

103
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:10,940
If a person has the
confidence or will to win,

104
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:13,807
their power can be
amplified many times over.

105
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:18,277
That's what makes Lena so powerful.

106
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:21,242
She's confident because
ever since she was a kid,

107
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,077
she had the best training
in swordsmanship.

108
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:27,980
So if you can imagine yourself
to be more powerful than anyone,

109
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:32,000
you'll have the potential to
rewrite the laws of this world.

110
00:07:50,020 --> 00:07:52,820
Oh, my God.

111
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:20,340
You win again, as always.

112
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:23,189
But you came close a
few times, didn't you?

113
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:24,960
No, it was all you.

114
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:26,637
Don't be so modest.

115
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:30,367
I know you still have some latent
power you're hiding from me.

116
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:32,260
One year ago,

117
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:37,580
I chose you for my page because I
sensed a similarity in our sword styles.

118
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:40,037
But over the course of the year,

119
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:44,537
it's become obvious how unrefined
my skills actually are. No way!

120
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:45,540
You're amazing!

121
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:49,900
In the end, I couldn't even beat
you once during our training.

122
00:08:51,060 --> 00:08:55,800
For two years, give or take, there is
someone I have not managed to beat either.

123
00:08:56,780 --> 00:09:00,060
Oh, you mean first seat Volo Leventayne.

124
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:03,370
Yes.

125
00:09:03,453 --> 00:09:07,940
Between you and I, whenever I face
him, I falter, just like a coward.

126
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,200
No matter how hard I train,

127
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:12,997
I can't seem to convince myself I have the

128
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:15,820
skill or the power to withstand his sword.

129
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:17,170
Lina.

130
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:21,517
However, it is not the same
for you when you face me.

131
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:26,340
There is more to the Aincrad style
that you haven't shown me, isn't there?

132
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:30,020
So before I graduate
the day after tomorrow,

133
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:33,280
I want to know everything
you're capable of.

134
00:09:37,380 --> 00:09:38,720
With this thing?

135
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:43,900
I will, but I can't right now. I'm sorry.

136
00:09:44,180 --> 00:09:47,945
But if you can wait till tomorrow,
I promise I'll show you then.

137
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:50,317
The greatest sword skill I can use.

138
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:52,760
But tomorrow's a day of rest.

139
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:54,777
You know training is forbidden then.

140
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:56,684
Yeah, but it won't be training.

141
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:58,037
It'll be your...

142
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,640
your graduation present.

143
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:00,920
Yeah, that's it.

144
00:10:01,140 --> 00:10:03,375
You can give presents on days of rest.

145
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:08,457
I've never heard of gifting sword
skills before, but if you insist...

146
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:11,660
Alright, I look forward to it. Awesome.

147
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:12,880
Tomorrow then.

148
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:34,117
Kirito is here, ma 'am!

149
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:35,788
I'm sorry I'm late, ma 'am.

150
00:10:35,980 --> 00:10:40,260
Why are you 38 minutes late, Primary
Trainee Kirito? Practicing, ma 'am.

151
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:42,820
With Elite Disciple Sordalina Surlute.

152
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:45,497
Our session went longer than usual today.

153
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:47,637
I applaud your commitment
to your education.

154
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:51,600
It is your duty as a page to
learn from your mentor. However,

155
00:10:51,980 --> 00:10:54,237
it seems to me that
you think your training

156
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:56,537
gives you permission to break your curfew.

157
00:10:56,620 --> 00:10:58,760
Oh, of course not, Mrs. Zerica.

158
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:02,595
All I want is to get better
as a swordsman, that's all.

159
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:05,995
Me coming in after curfew is
just an accident, I swear.

160
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:09,700
Mealtime is starting in 17 minutes.

161
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:12,079
Make sure you're not late for that.

162
00:11:13,620 --> 00:11:14,796
Where have you been?

163
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:18,160
Sorry, my sparring session
with Lina went long.

164
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:20,410
Yum!

165
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:30,500
I cannot tell you how
jealous I am, Lord Rios.

166
00:11:30,880 --> 00:11:33,960
After we toiled so hard
cleaning this cafeteria,

167
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:37,597
they get to just waltz in and
eat as if they own the place.

168
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,840
I so envy their good fortune.

169
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:42,140
Now, now, Umber, don't slander.

170
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:44,682
Pages have their struggles, too.

171
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:48,312
I'm sure their duties are
beyond what even we can imagine.

172
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:50,660
I suppose you're right.

173
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:54,077
These pages have to be at
their mentor's beck and call.

174
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:57,157
Why, I heard they have to
indulge their every whim.

175
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:59,877
Could you imagine what
it must be like for them,

176
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:02,257
having a mentor from a lower-class house?

177
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:04,869
They must issue the
most outlandish orders.

178
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:07,460
Ignore those two jerks. Just eat.

179
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:10,537
Oh, I've been meaning to ask.

180
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:12,444
How's your garden coming along?

181
00:12:14,620 --> 00:12:16,679
Doing pretty good so far, actually.

182
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:20,360
It should be in full bloom
in time for graduation. Nice.

183
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:21,875
Can't wait to see it.

184
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:30,637
They look like they're doing great.

185
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:32,426
They're even starting to bud.

186
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:36,036
It took three tries, but I
finally got the hang of it.

187
00:12:36,180 --> 00:12:38,356
Man, I really hope this batch blooms.

188
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:40,697
It's on course, too, by the looks of it.

189
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:43,637
They're going to make a wonderful
graduation gift for Lena.

190
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:44,955
You're so thoughtful.

191
00:12:46,380 --> 00:12:47,520
Give me a break.

192
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:50,517
After knowing you for the past two years,

193
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:53,541
I had no idea you liked
puttering around a garden.

194
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:56,960
Yeah, I'm as surprised
as you. You know what?

195
00:12:57,120 --> 00:13:00,037
This might be a sign that
your memories are coming back.

196
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:03,840
Maybe before you came to rule
it, you used to be a gardener.

197
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:06,820
Yeah, maybe that was your calling.

198
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:09,060
Uh, yeah, maybe.

199
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:11,265
I'm, uh, gonna get some water.

200
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:12,980
Wait, what?

201
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:17,860
At some point, you may end up
getting your memory back. What then?

202
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:19,710
Huh?

203
00:13:19,793 --> 00:13:20,623
What do you mean?

204
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,351
You're training to be an Integrity Knight.

205
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:26,405
But you're only here
because you're helping me.

206
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:30,840
I'm here because I want to find
Alice and bring her back home.

207
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:34,880
What if you remember your home?

208
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:45,437
If I do get my memory
back I ain't going home.

209
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,477
There's one thing I know.

210
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:48,977
I'm a swordsman.

211
00:13:49,060 --> 00:13:53,817
All the way for a swordsman being
an integrity knight's a dream job.

212
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:55,677
I'm weak.

213
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:57,417
I always have been.

214
00:13:57,500 --> 00:14:00,977
If I hadn't met you I don't know.

215
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:04,477
I guess I'd still be
swinging that axe right now.

216
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:06,600
Still stuck in my.

217
00:14:08,060 --> 00:14:09,797
village, blaming it all on my calling.

218
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:14,140
The only reason I'm even here
is because I had you with me

219
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,061
to lead the way.

220
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:17,697
It's all because of you.

221
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:21,620
And just now, when you said
you wouldn't return to your

222
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:27,620
home even if you got your memory back, it
filled me with such relief. Oh, come on.

223
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:29,060
Quit your moping.

224
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,897
You think I could have made it all
the way to the capital by myself?

225
00:14:32,980 --> 00:14:36,156
I didn't know where it was,
Plus, my memory's a blank.

226
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:39,820
And worse, I didn't have
two coins to rub together.

227
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:43,337
The only reason I'm here
now is because of you.

228
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:44,880
We make a great team.

229
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:47,040
So why mess that up?

230
00:14:47,340 --> 00:14:49,340
We're better if we stick together.

231
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:54,215
We can worry about going our own ways
after we become Integrity Knights.

232
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:55,190
Deal?

233
00:14:58,480 --> 00:14:59,360
Okay, deal.

234
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:02,657
First things first, though.

235
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:04,560
We have to ace this exam.

236
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:07,138
Only the top 12 will get to advance.

237
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:10,868
Yeah, well, I'm having a hard
time with my sacred art skills.

238
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:12,160
So what do you say?

239
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:14,285
Want to help your partner out?

240
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:15,660
Of course.

241
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:19,219
In fact, tomorrow's our day
of rest so we can study.

242
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:20,980
I can't.

243
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:22,540
Oh, right, I forgot.

244
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:25,280
Yep, tomorrow's the day I pick it up.

245
00:15:25,420 --> 00:15:26,655
I bet you're excited.

246
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:29,075
Hell yeah, I've been waiting all year.

247
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:30,660
Can't wait to try it out.

248
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:38,901
These things don't grow on trees.

249
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:42,611
A black brick rhinestone's
supposed to last me three years.

250
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:46,311
I went through six of them this
year working on that thing.

251
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,620
Uh, yeah, sorry about that.

252
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:53,941
That ranch was so tough, it took me a whole
damn day just to scrape a sliver off it.

253
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:58,320
You have any idea how many hours I
spent shaving away at this thing?

254
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:04,800
The tip of the Giga-seater is the part
that absorbed all the blessings of Solus

255
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:14,580
Take it on your journey And
when you reach the capital,

256
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:17,280
go and see Sardaray, the craftsman,

257
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:21,940
and leave it in his care He'll
make a wonderful sword from it

258
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,400
See that?

259
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:28,677
I'm a craftsman by calling but
metalsmithing's where my heart's really...

260
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:29,590
I'm sorry.

261
00:16:29,673 --> 00:16:30,680
Did you finish the sword?

262
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:38,600
Young man.

263
00:16:39,700 --> 00:16:43,000
I don't remember us
talking about money yet.

264
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:45,660
Don't worry. It's okay.

265
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,230
Pay the man.

266
00:16:47,313 --> 00:16:49,737
If you don't have enough,
I can loan you the rest.

267
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:51,977
Of course, I might let you just have it.

268
00:16:52,060 --> 00:16:54,100
Huh? Huh? Really? Really.

269
00:16:54,420 --> 00:16:55,437
But there's a catch.

270
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:58,108
You've got to be able
to swing this monster.

271
00:16:58,520 --> 00:16:59,500
Good luck.

272
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:03,995
When I finished, I tried picking it
up, and the damn thing felt heavier.

273
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:05,840
No way. It did?

274
00:17:19,180 --> 00:17:21,060
What's wrong? Draw it.

275
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:24,340
Okay, here goes.

276
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:52,760
Nice form, Kirito.

277
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:55,720
So a trainee can handle it.

278
00:17:56,020 --> 00:17:57,457
Well, now I've seen everything.

279
00:17:57,540 --> 00:17:58,720
It's a good sword.

280
00:17:59,020 --> 00:18:00,020
Damn right it is.

281
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:02,460
Anyway, the sword's all yours.

282
00:18:02,780 --> 00:18:04,662
I'm a man of my word, after all.

283
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:08,260
Thanks a lot!

284
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:12,752
Hey, I'm gonna go try this out for a bit.

285
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:15,920
Okay, just don't be late
for dinner. I won't.

286
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:29,860
This world's no game, but
it's got sword skills.

287
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:34,080
I can only do two-hit combos
with my practice sword.

288
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:36,560
Let's see what this can do.

289
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,540
This is great.

290
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:50,800
I can keep my promise to Lena now.

291
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:53,600
No, wait, how about a five-parter?

292
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:57,140
The blue rose sword couldn't
do one, but maybe this can.

293
00:19:11,940 --> 00:19:13,800
I guess it can't.

294
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,580
First Seat Levantain.

295
00:19:26,340 --> 00:19:28,580
I'm sorry, Elite Disciple Levantain.

296
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:31,400
I didn't mean to get dirt on your uniform.

297
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:33,200
I've seen you before.

298
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:36,380
You're Elite Disciple
Sirloot's page. Yes, sir.

299
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:37,960
Primary Trainee Kirito.

300
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:39,750
Right.

301
00:19:39,833 --> 00:19:42,340
Practicing the sword is
forbidden on a day of rest.

302
00:19:42,540 --> 00:19:44,380
I, um, I wasn't.

303
00:19:44,540 --> 00:19:46,011
This isn't practice, sir.

304
00:19:46,620 --> 00:19:49,360
Um, I was just trying out my new sword.

305
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:51,445
I couldn't wait till tomorrow.

306
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:55,900
Your test swings were, how
shall I say, enthusiastic.

307
00:19:57,340 --> 00:20:00,020
You and I are similar that way.

308
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:06,220
We both search for a reason to wield
a sword, even on a day of rest.

309
00:20:06,940 --> 00:20:10,660
Yearning to scratch
that itch. You too? Yes.

310
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:13,640
So I shall overlook that transgression.

311
00:20:13,940 --> 00:20:15,469
You're very generous, sir.

312
00:20:15,820 --> 00:20:19,900
Do not thank me yet,
Trainee Kirito. Uh, pardon?

313
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:23,640
I did not say I would
forgive you for this.

314
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:32,780
News travels fast.

315
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:34,870
Kirito!

316
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:38,440
What'd you do this time? Nothing.

317
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:42,020
Oh, well, it was a good run.

318
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:45,737
You survived a whole year here
without getting into trouble.

319
00:20:45,820 --> 00:20:47,400
New record, partner.

320
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:51,000
Lord Levantain, what
is the meaning of this?

321
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:52,940
Just a minor infraction.

322
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:55,540
Your page was disrespectful to me.

323
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:58,737
Nothing that demands serious
punishment, mind you.

324
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:01,820
So we shall settle it by
sparring with real swords.

325
00:21:01,980 --> 00:21:02,980
What did you say?

326
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:05,457
You don't have to worry about me, ma 'am.

327
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:07,680
Really, I can handle myself.

328
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:13,122
In fact, I sort of feel honored to get the
chance to spar with the first seed here.

329
00:21:13,300 --> 00:21:16,097
Kirito, have you discussed
the rules with him yet?

330
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:20,220
No, but since we're using real
swords, isn't it stopped short?

331
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:22,615
I forgot to mention something earlier.

332
00:21:22,700 --> 00:21:25,440
I do not engage in shortstop duels.

333
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:29,920
For all my personal matches, I
prefer to fight first strike.

334
00:21:30,180 --> 00:21:32,437
He's never fought a
match with real swords.

335
00:21:32,520 --> 00:21:34,097
Besides, you need his consent.

336
00:21:34,180 --> 00:21:35,720
Of course, mine too.

337
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:38,512
This cannot proceed unless we both agree.

338
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:42,260
And if he does not, the
match will be stopped short.

339
00:21:43,020 --> 00:21:45,620
Well, trainee Kirito, do you agree?

340
00:21:46,220 --> 00:21:48,960
Don't do it, Kirito. Lolo's strong.

341
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:50,240
He will hurt you.

342
00:21:51,020 --> 00:21:54,180
I think I'll let you
decide it, Lord Levantain.

343
00:21:54,600 --> 00:21:56,776
I'm the one being punished after all.

344
00:22:23,580 --> 00:22:26,820
Let's do it.

345
00:23:35,780 --> 00:23:38,380
Next time, Swordsman's Pride.

346
00:23:39,060 --> 00:23:41,600
Thank you.
